      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "NbMoTaW has excellent mechanical performance at 1600 °C.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "NbMoTaW has very poor room-temperature ductility.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The irradiation resistance of NbMoTaW has been predicted by first-principles calculations.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention is to introduce up to about 10 at.% V by substituting an unspecified NbMoTaW constituent.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A V addition of up to about 10 at.% will slightly expand the BCC lattice.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The V addition will modify local stacking-fault energies.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lattice and stacking-fault-energy changes caused by V will lower the energy barrier for dislocation movement.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "V has a sufficiently similar atomic size and chemical character to lower the Peierls barrier in NbMoTaW.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A lower Peierls barrier will increase dislocation mobility and room-temperature plasticity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Keeping the V concentration at or below about 10 at.% will preserve single-phase BCC stability.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "V-modified NbMoTaW will exhibit greater room-temperature plastic strain before fracture than untreated NbMoTaW.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "V-modified NbMoTaW will retain approximately the high-temperature mechanical performance of untreated NbMoTaW at 1600 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Low-concentration V will preserve defect-recombination characteristics and leave irradiation resistance unchanged.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
